 "_": "His Rhone's water, measured (DESIGN 5.2, 5.3). Not a density in the world but a coverage on the canvas: the share of the water his paint covers, and every measure of a mark against the spacing between marks, which is the square root of the water's area over the number of marks. A mark's lie is how far off horizontal it is on his canvas, and horizontal on a water seen from a bank is across the line of sight, which is the way a wave's front lies. Ours lie across the drift of the wind for the same reason, and that is the one thing in this hand that is a person's reading of it.",
